              "raw_utf8": "{\"checks\":[{\"command\":\"python3 -B public_check.py\",\"outcome\":\"not_run\"}],\"clarification\":\"No shell/execution tool was provided in this session's toolset, so I could not actually run the required public_check.py command; please run it to confirm, or grant shell access so I can verify.\",\"diagnosis\":\"write_headers() in h11/_writers.py was serialising the lower-cased header name instead of the caller-supplied raw_name, discarding original casing. Additionally, set_comma_header() in h11/_headers.py always used its lower-case-only name argument both for matching and for writing new entries, so server-generated framing headers (Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding, Connection) were emitted all-lowercase. Fixed by: (1) write_headers now writes raw_name for both the Host-first pass and the remaining headers, keeping the lower-cased name only for the Host comparison; (2) set_comma_header now matches existing headers via name.lower() but preserves whatever casing is passed in for newly written values; (3) _connection.py's _clean_up_response_headers_for_sending now calls set_comma_header with conventionally-cased names (Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding, Connection) so generated framing headers have consistent, readable spelling while get_comma_header lookups remain lower-case and unaffected.\",\"evidence\":[\"h11/_writers.py write_headers now uses raw_name in both write() calls instead of the lower-cased name\",\"h11/_headers.py set_comma_header now compares found_name != name.lower() and appends (name, new_value) preserving caller casing\",\"h11/_connection.py _clean_up_response_headers_for_sending now passes b'Content-Length', b'Transfer-Encoding', b'Connection' to set_comma_header instead of lower-case variants\",\"Host-first ordering in write_headers is preserved since the comparison still uses the lower-cased name field\"],\"remaining\":[\"Run python3 -B public_check.py in an environment with shell access to confirm the fix passes the acceptance contract, since no execution tool was available in this session.\"],\"status\":\"partial\"}",
              "report": {
