                "diagnosis": "write_headers() in h11/_writers.py was serialising the lower-cased header name instead of the caller-supplied raw_name, discarding original casing. Additionally, set_comma_header() in h11/_headers.py always used its lower-case-only name argument both for matching and for writing new entries, so server-generated framing headers (Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding, Connection) were emitted all-lowercase. Fixed by: (1) write_headers now writes raw_name for both the Host-first pass and the remaining headers, keeping the lower-cased name only for the Host comparison; (2) set_comma_header now matches existing headers via name.lower() but preserves whatever casing is passed in for newly written values; (3) _connection.py's _clean_up_response_headers_for_sending now calls set_comma_header with conventionally-cased names (Content-Length, Transfer-Encoding, Connection) so generated framing headers have consistent, readable spelling while get_comma_header lookups remain lower-case and unaffected.",
